  "body": "## Change\n\nAC rotary travel errors report the zero-based index of the original input move. The typed cause keeps the blocking axis, required angle, travel limits, and hint. The index refers to the input before subdivision.\n\nThis gives a future post a way to locate an input move, revise it, and ask the engine to solve and validate the revised path. The solver applies its existing travel and continuity checks.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The quick gate passed 16 steps on `bddd6d7e4` against `034e91b8b`. All 254 tests passed across 14 suites.\n- The AC path safety suite passed all 13 tests. It pins the original index with `initial_pose_travel_refusal_names_move_zero`, `rotary_travel_refusal_names_the_original_move`, and `subdivision_travel_refusal_names_the_original_move`.\n- The catalog suites passed. `example_catalog` passed 43 tests. `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work` each passed one test.\n- The branch trial-merges cleanly with upstream main at `5b52c5f8c`. Independent local source review returned zero findings on the final head.\n- Verification used synthetic solver paths and shipped examples. Hardware execution is outside the test scope. The light gate and CamCraft collaborator review are pending.\n\nFork synced at v0.26.0. The change branch is based on upstream main at `034e91b8b`.\n\nChangelog: Name the original move in AC rotary travel refusals.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3841",
